TensorFold patch 0005: Flash Next's concurrent decoder keeps every conversation's latest prompt end.

Why: with several agent conversations at once, their follow-up turns stopped reusing the prefix cache (2026-10-12:
4 conversations, one follow-up fully cold; 8 conversations x 4 turns: 0% of the follow-up prompt tokens reused, 13-26 s
to the first token of a 5.8k-token prompt instead of ~0.4 s). The kept prompt ends (resume points, KEEP = 8 for all
conversations) were dropped oldest first; each turn adds 2-3 (its message starts and its end), so a conversation that
was waiting lost all of its points and its slot went back to the free list.

What:
- prefixes.py remember: over the cap, the oldest point of a slot that keeps a newer one goes first, so each slot keeps
  its latest point while any slot has an older one to give; then the oldest, as before.
- engine.py: KEEP from TF_FLASH_KEEP (default 8, as upstream; ~115 MB of DeltaNet state a point for Flash Next,
  counted by the admission). The recipe sets 16 with STREAMS=8 (8 conversations keep a slot each).

Base: TensorFold 609ca419 + the recipe's vision-prefix-cache.patch + local 0001-0004.

